From efd19216376af93b94c48b356166b0a2f81d63d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (developer)" <dev@meetfa.local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:25:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(content): captions stop updating after a pause (stage
 2.1)

Root cause (reproduced in DOM simulation, not yet confirmed in real Meet):
SegmentTracker ignored every update to a block element once its segment
was final. Meet keeps the same block element while the same speaker
continues, so after >=4s silence (idle finalize) all further text of that
block was dropped.

- segmentTracker: continuation of a finalized block goes to a new segment
  (final segments stay immutable); continuationAfter() handles growth,
  head-trim and ASR tail revisions without duplicates
- captionObserver: status reflects real text flow (capturing only when text
  is recorded; silence => ready, never error); evidence-based error when Meet
  shows new text but nothing is recorded for 3 scans; re-attach if a new
  caption region replaces a still-connected old one; debug logs
- sidepanel: last-received time; refresh hint after install/update
- tests: 8 regression tests (6 fail on 9e7292c); docs/manual-test-captions.md
